DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aalltteerraa__jjttaagg__uuaarrtt device driver provides support for the Altera JTAG
     UART core, which allows multiple UART-like streams to be carried over
     JTAG.  aalltteerraa__jjttaagg__uuaarrtt allows JTAG UART streams to be attached to both
     the low-level console interface, used for direct kernel input and output,
     and the tty(4) layer, to be used with ttys(5) and login(1).  Sequential
     Altera JTAG UART devices will appear as ttyu0, ttyu1, etc.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     Altera JTAG UART devices can be connected to using Altera's
     _n_i_o_s_2_-_t_e_r_m_i_n_a_l program, with the instance selected using the --instance
     argument on the management host.  aalltteerraa__jjttaagg__uuaarrtt supports JTAG UART
     cores with or without interrupt lines connected; if the irq portion of
     the _d_e_v_i_c_e_._h_i_n_t_s entry is omitted, the driver will poll rather than con‐
     figure interrupts.

